each covered carrier may provide subsequent updates, including flight status changes, as the carrier
deems appropriate;
(7) For all departing flights and diversions, each time the opportunity to deplane exists at a suitable
disembarkation point, each covered carrier must timely notify the passengers on board the aircraft
that the passengers have the opportunity to deplane;

